%N A401885 Decimal expansion of the area of the pentagon egg constructed from a regular pentagon of side length 1.
%C A401885 The side length is that of the outer pentagon. In cyclic order the four tangent arcs have radii 1/phi^2, 1, 1/phi^3, 1 and central angles Pi, Pi/5, 3*Pi/5, Pi/5, where phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2.
%C A401885 Their chords form a trapezoid with bases 2/phi^2 and 1/phi^2 and height sin(Pi/5). The area is the area of the trapezoid plus the four circular segment areas r^2*(theta-sin(theta))/2.
%H A401885 Cyrille Dumoutier, <a href="https://art-et-tonneaux.fr/blog/video-geometrie-baignoire-ove-pentagone-n81">Géométrie : L'œuf du pentagone</a>, Art et Tonneaux, May 06 2021.
%H A401885 Numberphile, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CoJtruAGfTY">Drawing an Egg (with a Pentagon)</a>, featuring Johnny Ball.
%H A401885 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Egg.html">Egg</a>.
%H A401885 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PentagonEgg.html">Pentagon Egg</a>.
%F A401885 Equals (3*Pi*(5*phi-4)-20*sin(Pi/5))/(10*phi^3), where phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2.
%e A401885 0.63250256223734657874283957231705159052026488166907...
%t A401885 First[RealDigits[(3 Pi (5 GoldenRatio - 4) - 20 Sin[Pi/5])/(10 GoldenRatio^3), 10, 87]]
%Y A401885 Cf. A376642 (area of Moss's egg).
